---
title: Multi-Hop
description: Chain through intermediate relays to reach targets that cannot connect directly.
order: 8
---

# Multi-Hop

Some targets sit behind a host that can reach your machine, but the target itself cannot. A relay in the middle bridges the gap — the DMZ host (`10.0.1.10`) connects out to your machine (`10.0.0.5`) and listens inward for the next hop.

{% steps %}
{% step title="Attacker (Entry)" number=1 %}
Listen for the first hop.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="DMZ Host (Relay)" number=2 %}
Connect to the attacker and listen for the next hop.

{% codeblock code="./wallhack relay --connect 10.0.0.5:443 --listen :6565" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Internal Host (Exit)" number=3 %}
Connect back to the relay.

{% codeblock code="./wallhack exit --connect 10.0.1.10:6565" /%}
{% /step %}

{% step title="Configure Routes" number=4 %}
Route the internal networks through the tunnel.

```bash
ip route add 192.168.1.0/24 dev tun0
ip route add 192.168.2.0/24 dev tun0
```
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}

{% trafficflow flow="10.0.0.5 (you) -> 10.0.1.10 (DMZ) -> internal host -> 192.168.1.0/24, 192.168.2.0/24" label="Traffic Flow:" /%}
